From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] engine: new workbooks are Times New Roman 12 pt with 15.75 pt
 rows; their sheets print on A4 in an Uzbek or Russian interface

Owner decisions 2026-10-29 (docs/phase4/design-system.md, "Revised"; Q6): a new workbook's Normal font is Times New Roman 12 pt, with the 15.75 pt (21 px) default row height Excel gives that font; its sheets print on A4 in an Uzbek or Russian interface and on Letter in English (from the number locale, which follows the interface language). The desktop app makes the blank Book1 after the preferences, once that language is known. Insert Sheet takes the active sheet's paper and the Normal font's row height. Automatic row heights compare sizes with the workbook's Normal font instead of a fixed 11 pt, so 12 pt text keeps the default row (files with an 11 pt Normal font behave as before). Opened files keep their own fonts, rows and paper.
